<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Hardened-runtime entitlements for Kod (ai.felis.kod), Developer ID distribution.
       Intentionally EMPTY. This is not a placeholder — it is the measured answer.

       EDITING THIS COMMENT: never write a double dash inside it. XML forbids one
       anywhere in a comment except its own terminator, so spell command flags
       without their leading dashes. `plutil -lint` is lenient and reports this
       file OK either way; AMFI's parser is not, and codesign dies with
       "AMFIUnserializeXML: syntax error near line N" — which reads like a broken
       plist rather than a broken sentence. It cost one signing failure already.

       Under codesign's hardened runtime (its `options runtime` flag) macOS blocks
       JIT / unsigned executable memory, blocks DYLD_* env injection, and enforces
       Library Validation. Kod trips none of those:
         - No embedded JIT / WASM / JS runtime (no wasmtime, cranelift, v8, quickjs
           in the dep tree). GPUI renders via blade-graphics -> Metal; Metal shader
           compilation runs OUT OF PROCESS (MTLCompilerService), so no allow-jit /
           allow-unsigned-executable-memory is required.
         - Only Apple-signed frameworks are loaded (Metal, AppKit, Foundation);
           Rust links statically, so Library Validation stays on (no
           disable-library-validation).
         - NO App Sandbox: Developer-ID (non-App-Store) distribution does not need
           it, and it would break orchestrator-daemon's $TMPDIR Unix socket and its
           CLI subprocess spawning. Do NOT add com.apple.security.app-sandbox.
         - UserNotifications (UNUserNotificationCenter) needs NO entitlement for
           LOCAL notifications — only a signed, bundled app with a stable bundle id,
           which ai.felis.kod + make-app.sh already provide. aps-environment is for
           REMOTE/push only and is intentionally absent.

       Add an entry below ONLY if a launch crash or a notarization/crash log proves
       it is needed (the sign + `notarytool submit` with its wait flag + launch is
       measurement that settles it):
         - EXC_BAD_ACCESS / mprotect fault mapping executable memory at first frame
           (some Metal driver paths) ->
             <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key><true/>
             <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key><true/>
         - a dlopen of a non-Apple dylib blocked at runtime (only if the dormant
           Vulkan/ash path ever activates on macOS) ->
             <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key><true/>
  -->
</dict>
</plist>
